# Fixed network roles (NanoPC-T6 + Mid-360)

Do **not** change these roles unless the user explicitly asks:

| Interface role | Env | Address | Notes |
|----------------|-----|---------|-------|
| Ethernet | `LIDAR_INTERFACE` | host `192.168.1.50/24` | Mid-360 only, `never-default` |
| Mid-360 | `LIDAR_IP` | `192.168.1.1XX` | XX = serial last two digits; `.env` example `192.168.1.12` is a placeholder |
| WiFi STA | `LAN_INTERFACE` | DHCP from existing router | Local SSH / LAN only, not default route |
| 4G | `WAN_INTERFACE` | carrier DHCP | Default route; MyView `/ws/lidar` (`MYVIEW_VIA=wan`) |

`PC_IP` means the **lidar ethernet** address as seen by Mid-360 (`192.168.1.50`), not the WiFi IP.

If WiFi LAN is also `192.168.1.0/24`, move the lidar subnet (Viewer 2 + `LIDAR_IP` / `PC_IP` / `LIDAR_SUBNET`) rather than merging the two.

T6 `eth0`/`eth1` can swap across reboots — pin by PCI/MAC before hard-coding `LIDAR_INTERFACE`.
